<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Android 12+ splash icon: the same white flame on the brand red background.

    Two things differ from a naive copy of the flame path.

    First, the fill is white. The background is the brand red (#FE2C55) set by splash_bg, and a red flame
    on a red background is invisible - which is what the old file produced, because it kept the red fill
    while values-v31 painted the background white. The two halves of the splash had drifted apart.

    Second, the flame is scaled down inside the 24x24 viewport. Android 12 masks this icon with a circle
    roughly two thirds of its box, and the flame path spans y 0.67..22 - almost the full height - so the
    top of the flame and the flat base were being clipped off. Scaling to 0.58 about the flame's own
    centre (12, 11.335) keeps every edge inside the mask.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <group
        android:pivotX="12"
        android:pivotY="11.335"
        android:scaleX="0.58"
        android:scaleY="0.58">
